  description: Moscovium is the name of a synthetic superheavy element in the periodic
    table that has the symbol Mc and has the atomic number 115. It is an extremely
    radioactive element; its most stable known isotope, moscovium-289, has a half-life
    of only 220 milliseconds. It is also known as eka-bismuth or simply element 115.
